http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Naming_artifacts

Imagine, you're at mines' end. You find a gray stone. You want to
#name it as an individual object "The Heart of Ahriman" and get the
following messages:
 While engraving your hand slips.
 You engrave: "Tve Heart of Ahriman".

Now you know that you're gray stone is a luckstone. If you can #name
it without hand-slipping, it isn't a luckstone.

This bug has to do with how artifacts are programmed. They are more or
less just specially named objects and then it's clear that you are not
allowed to name one yourself.

